WEBVTT

00:03:59.933 --> 00:04:02.767
on the scale of anything that matters
for everyday life.

00:04:02.791 --> 00:04:05.123
And then there's cosmology,
which is up there;

00:04:05.147 --> 00:04:06.458
very large, very far away,

00:04:06.482 --> 00:04:08.482
also very weird.

00:04:08.506 --> 00:04:10.506
And if you go to some places

00:04:10.530 --> 00:04:13.594
like black holes
in the beginning of the universe,

00:04:13.618 --> 00:04:16.620
we know that these are frontiers
in physics, right?

00:04:16.644 --> 00:04:19.399
There's lots of work being done
to discover new physics

00:04:19.423 --> 00:04:20.849
in these places.

00:04:21.317 --> 00:04:24.834
But the thing is, you will notice
there's a very large gap in the middle.

00:04:24.858 --> 00:04:27.016
And in that gap, there are many things.

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:29.683
There are planets and toasts
and volcanoes and clouds

00:04:29.707 --> 00:04:31.844
and clarinets and bubbles and dolphins